@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<p class="text-muted">Last updated: October 20, 2026</p>

<p>
    This policy explains what personal information the library2 system collects, why it is collected,
    and how it is handled. By using this system, you acknowledge the practices described below.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">1. Information we collect</h2>
<p>The system stores only the information needed to run the library:</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Member records:</strong> full name, email address (optional), member type
        (Regular, Student, or Faculty), and the date you joined.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Loan records:</strong> which books a member borrowed, the date borrowed,
        the number of days allowed, and the date returned.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Book records:</strong> title, category, and price. These are not personal information.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    The system does not use accounts or passwords, and it does not use advertising or tracking cookies.
    Like most web servers, it may keep technical logs (such as request time and error details) for troubleshooting.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">2. How we use your information</h2>
<ul>
    <li>To register members and manage borrowing and returns.</li>
    <li>To contact members about their loans, when an email address is provided.</li>
    <li>To keep basic library statistics, such as how many books are on loan.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your information or use it for marketing.</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">3. Where your information is stored</h2>
<p>
    Library data is stored in a PostgreSQL database hosted by a third-party provider (Supabase).
    Access to the database is limited to authorized library staff and administrators.
    The provider may process data on servers outside your country.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">4. Sharing your information</h2>
<p>
    Your information is shared only with library staff who need it to do their work, with the hosting provider
    that stores the data, and where disclosure is required by law.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">5. How long we keep your information</h2>
<p>
    Member and loan records are kept while your membership is active and for as long as needed for library
    record-keeping. When a member record is deleted, it is removed from the system. A member who still has loan
    records cannot be deleted until those records are resolved.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">6. Your rights</h2>
<p>You may ask the library to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>show you the information stored about you;</li>
    <li>correct information that is wrong or out of date (for example, your name or email);</li>
    <li>delete your member record, where no loan records prevent it.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    If you are in the Philippines, you also have the rights provided under the Data Privacy Act of 2012
    (Republic Act No. 10173), including the right to be informed, to access, to correct, and to object.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">7. Security</h2>
<p>
    We use reasonable measures to protect your information, including encrypted connections to the database
    and restricted access. No system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last changed.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">9. Contact us</h2>
<p>
    For questions or requests about your information, contact the library administrator at
    <strong>[your name or office]</strong>, <strong>[your email address]</strong>.
</p>
